Room: HTTP and proxy authentication of Room pages goes to the host.

Chrome asks for credentials in a Views dialog (LoginHandlerViews, tab-modal
over its BrowserView). A Room page's challenge belongs to the host's sign-in
sheet (the Engine protocol's didReceiveAuthChallenge, Phase 2.6a). Chrome's
own flow around it stays: HttpAuthCoordinator, the extensions'
onAuthRequired, LoginTabHelper's committed error page, the password
manager's HTTP auth observer and "another handler supplied the same
credentials".

No existing hook: LoginHandler::Create is the platform factory, defined once
per UI toolkit (this file on desktop) and called by HttpAuthCoordinator and
LoginTabHelper; ContentBrowserClient::CreateLoginDelegate belongs to
ChromeContentBrowserClient. //room returns a LoginHandler subclass only for
pages it wraps whose delegate answers challenges; everything else keeps
Chrome's dialog.

Phase 3.4a, 2026-10-05. //room: room/core/room_page_prompts.mm
(RoomLoginHandler).
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/login_handler_views.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/login_handler_views.cc
index 14a99f40f3109..9edcfaca38181 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/login_handler_views.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/login_handler_views.cc
@@ -22,6 +22,16 @@
 #include "ui/views/widget/widget.h"
 #include "ui/views/window/dialog_delegate.h"
 
+namespace room {
+// Room: set by //room/core at startup. Returns the host's handler for an
+// authentication challenge of a page in a Room window (the host's sign-in
+// sheet), nullptr otherwise (the callback is then untouched).
+std::unique_ptr<LoginHandler> (*g_create_login_handler_hook)(
+    const net::AuthChallengeInfo&,
+    content::WebContents*,
+    content::LoginDelegate::LoginAuthRequiredCallback&) = nullptr;
+}  // namespace room
+
 class LoginHandlerViewsDialog;
 
 namespace {
@@ -231,6 +241,12 @@ std::unique_ptr<LoginHandler> LoginHandler::Create(
     const net::AuthChallengeInfo& auth_info,
     content::WebContents* web_contents,
     content::LoginDelegate::LoginAuthRequiredCallback auth_required_callback) {
+  if (room::g_create_login_handler_hook) {
+    if (auto handler = room::g_create_login_handler_hook(
+            auth_info, web_contents, auth_required_callback)) {
+      return handler;
+    }
+  }
   return std::make_unique<LoginHandlerViews>(auth_info, web_contents,
                                              std::move(auth_required_callback));
 }
